!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
In its own file
description: a text file holding one scalar — the format carries the material type
- >
  A string may be a whole file: the text-material modeling. Markdown, asciidoc, csv, plantuml — any
  non-data text — is a `file/yaml` scalar whose single value is the raw text, kept verbatim; the
  `format` (`text/markdown`, `text/x-plantuml`) carries the real material type and selects the
  renderer. The concrete only records "a text file holding one scalar", so the same modeling covers
  every material the system will ever meet.
